# EXPERIMENT 4 – STATIC ROUTING CONFIGURATION

## 1. Aim
To configure static routing between two different networks using two routers.

## 2. Devices Required
- 2 Routers (R1 and R2)
- 2 Switches (S1 and S2)
- 4 PCs
- Copper Straight-Through cables
- 1 Serial DCE cable

## 3. Network Design

Create two LAN networks and one WAN connection:

- LAN A: `192.168.10.0/24`
- LAN B: `192.168.20.0/24`
- WAN: `10.10.10.0/8`

Connect:
- PC0 and PC1 to Switch S1.
- Switch S1 to R1 FastEthernet 0/0.
- PC2 and PC3 to Switch S2.
- Switch S2 to R2 FastEthernet 0/0.
- Connect R1 Serial 2/0 to R2 Serial 2/0 using Serial DCE.

## 4. PC IP Address Configuration

| Device | IP Address | Subnet Mask | Gateway |
|---|---|---|---|
| PC0 | 192.168.10.2 | 255.255.255.0 | 192.168.10.1 |
| PC1 | 192.168.10.3 | 255.255.255.0 | 192.168.10.1 |
| PC2 | 192.168.20.4 | 255.255.255.0 | 192.168.20.1 |
| PC3 | 192.168.20.2 | 255.255.255.0 | 192.168.20.1 |

Configure these using Desktop → IP Configuration → Static.

## 5. Router R1 Configuration

Open R1 → CLI.

```text
enable
configure terminal

interface fastethernet 0/0
ip address 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit

interface serial 2/0
ip address 10.10.10.1 255.0.0.0
clock rate 64000
no shutdown
exit

ip route 192.168.20.0 255.255.255.0 serial 2/0

end
write memory
```

Note: Enter `clock rate 64000` only on the DCE end of the serial connection. If R1 is not the DCE end, configure the clock rate on R2 instead.

## 6. Router R2 Configuration

Open R2 → CLI.

```text
enable
configure terminal

interface fastethernet 0/0
ip address 192.168.20.1 255.255.255.0
no shutdown
exit

interface serial 2/0
ip address 10.10.10.2 255.0.0.0
no shutdown
exit

ip route 192.168.10.0 255.255.255.0 10.10.10.1

end
write memory
```

## 7. Verify Static Routing

On R1 and R2:

```text
show ip interface brief
show ip route
```

In the routing table:
- `C` means Connected route.
- `S` means Static route.

## 8. Testing

From PC1:

```text
ping 192.168.20.2
```

From PC3:

```text
ping 192.168.10.2
```

Both pings should succeed after the interfaces and routes are correctly configured.

You can also use Simulation Mode to observe packet movement between the two LANs.

## 9. Expected Result

Static routes are successfully configured, allowing communication between the two different LAN networks.

